<PageLayout title="About Shelf Made Home" description="Shelf Made Home shares practical organization ideas for small kitchens, pantries and cabinets.">
  <p>Shelf Made Home is about one thing: making small kitchens easier to live with.</p>
  <p>Most kitchens aren't the ones in magazines. They have one awkward corner cabinet, a pantry that is really just a shelf, and a counter that fills up by Tuesday. This blog collects ideas that work in those kitchens: simple storage fixes, pantry systems that stay tidy, and the few products that are actually worth the space they take up.</p>
  <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Small kitchen organization ideas you can set up in an afternoon</li>
    <li>Pantry and cabinet systems that are easy to keep up</li>
    <li>Renter-friendly upgrades with no drilling</li>
    <li>Honest notes on storage products and what each one is good for</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How this blog is funded</h2>
  <p>Some posts link to products on Amazon. If you buy through those links, I may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. It never changes what I recommend. The details are on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> page.</p>
  <p>You can find more ideas every day on <a href={PINTEREST_URL}>Pinterest</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
